[{:adr/id "2607122145"
  :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-6202 (Computer consultancy and computer facilities management activities, CRM-integrated customer-service-hub actor) implemented"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-12"
  :db/id -1
  :adr/implements "cloud-itonami-isic-6202"
  :adr/related ["cloud-itonami-isic-5820 (names this build in its own docs/business-model.md sibling-actor roadmap)" "2607121900-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-crm-coverage (direct model)" "cloud-itonami-isic-6209 (distinct sibling, differentiated)" "cloud-itonami-isic-8220 (distinct sibling, differentiated)" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage (double-guard lesson source)" "kotoba-lang/crm (technical commons reused, 2nd consumer)" "langgraph-clj ADR-0001"]
  :adr/context "cloud-itonami-isic-5820 (ADR-2607121900) named two not-yet-built sibling actors in its own docs/business-model.md roadmap: a marketing-automation hub and a customer-service hub (support cases, SLAs, knowledge base), explicitly noting the customer-service hub is distinct from cloud-itonami-isic-6209's IT-helpdesk ticket routing (no CRM/subscription linkage) since it is account/subscription-aware. This ADR implements the customer-service hub. Investigation of kotoba-lang/industry's registry found ISIC 6201 already reserved for the marketing-automation sibling (kotoba-lang/crm's own README already documented cloud-itonami-isic-6201 as the marketing-automation consumer of kotoba.crm.pipeline/leadscore, confirming a concurrent session was building it), so a different ISIC code was needed for the customer-service hub."
  :adr/isic-selection-process "Surveyed ISIC divisions 58/62/63 (software/IT/data) and 82 (business support) 4-digit classes in kotoba-lang/industry's registry.edn. Excluded: 5820 (claimed, CRM), 6201 (reserved for marketing-automation sibling, concurrent build), 6209 (claimed, IT-helpdesk ticket routing), 6311/6312/6399 (claimed, distinct businesses), 8219/8220/8291/8299 (claimed, distinct businesses). Among remaining unclaimed :spec entries, selected ISIC 6202 'Computer consultancy and computer facilities management activities' -- the UNSD ISIC Rev.4 explanatory note for class 6202 (classification detail, code 6202) explicitly includes 'provision of on-site management and operation of clients' computer systems and/or data processing facilities, plus related support services'; narrowed the 'related support services' clause to a hosted, multi-tenant customer-service-hub SaaS platform (operating a client business's support desk as a facility). Other unclaimed candidates considered and rejected: 6391 (news agency, unrelated), 8211 (combined office administrative services -- reception/billing/mail, not case/SLA/KB management), 8230 (conventions/trade shows, unrelated), 8292 (packaging, unrelated), 8412 (health/education regulation, unrelated)."
  :adr/pattern-6202 "sealed SupportOps-LLM advisor + independent ServiceGovernor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on cloud-itonami-isic-5820, narrowed from ISIC 6202 'Computer consultancy and computer facilities management activities' to a CRM/subscription-integrated customer-service-hub SaaS platform business (HubSpot Service Hub/Salesforce Service Cloud-class)"
  :adr/distinctive-checks-6202 "sla-tier-gate (a case status transition must not itself commit a response-time promise faster than the account's active subscription/SLA tier entitles -- direct analog of -isic-5820's entitlement-scope-gate, genuinely new check kind for response-time commitments) and case-status-sequence-gate (rejects skipping/reversing the support-case lifecycle, reusing kotoba-lang/crm's kotoba.crm.pipeline as its 2nd consumer after -isic-5820) are the two domain-unique HARD checks. kb-embargo-gate (SOFT, always-escalate -- an embargoed knowledge-base article publish always reaches a human, a genuinely new check kind: content-embargo risk) and refund-commitment-gate (SOFT, always-escalate -- a case commitment implying a refund/credit always reaches a human) round out the governor alongside dispute-request (SOFT, unconditional, any phase)."
  :adr/guard-design-6202 "double-close-gate uses a dedicated :closed? boolean fact rather than a :status value, the same design choice ADR-2607071351 (cloud-itonami-isic-6920's status-lifecycle bug) and -isic-5820 (ADR-2607121900) established"
  :adr/differentiation-from-siblings "cloud-itonami-isic-6209 (TicketRouter-LLM sealed advisor, IT managed-services/helpdesk ticket routing) has no account/subscription entity at all -- routes by technician access-tier/certification only. cloud-itonami-isic-8220 (activities of call centres) is a staffing/BPO services business, not a software product -- registers/dispatches human agents for a client's call campaigns. This actor is the opposite emphasis: every support case is tied to a paying account's subscription tier, and the SLA a case may be promised is a function of that entitlement, never a technician's certification; it is a SaaS platform a business buys/self-hosts to run its OWN support desk, not a staffing agency."
  :adr/technical-commons-reused "kotoba.crm.pipeline (kotoba-lang/crm, generic ordered-stage transition validator factored out by cloud-itonami-isic-5820) drives case-status-sequence-gate for the support-case lifecycle (:new -> :in-progress -> :resolved -> :closed plus :cancelled exit), directly analogous to -isic-5820's sales-pipeline stage shape -- the 2nd consumer proving kotoba-lang/crm's shared-technical-commons design intent. kotoba.crm.revrec and kotoba.crm.leadscore are NOT used (out of scope: no revenue recognition or lead scoring responsibility)."
  :adr/no-west-manifest-registration "Deliberately did NOT register the new repo in this superproject's manifest/west.yml, following the same established convention ADR-2607121900 confirmed: none of the 140+ existing :implemented cloud-itonami-isic-#### actors are registered there."
  :adr/registry-landing-method "kotoba-lang/industry's registry.edn '6202' entry (:maturity :spec with a stale gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J6202 placeholder repo) was promoted to :implemented via the GitHub Contents API (fetch tip sha/content -> edit only the 6202 entry's lines -> PUT with sha=) as a single atomic commit, the fleet's established race-safe pattern for concurrent registry writes. Diff confirmed limited to exactly the 6202 entry (46 lines) before committing, verifying no collision with concurrent sibling promotions (e.g. the marketing-automation ADR-2607122130 landing around the same time)."
  :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 144}"
  :adr/test-status-6202 "clojure -M:dev:test: 33 tests / 110 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. clojure -M:lint (clj-kondo): 0 errors / 0 warnings. clojure -M:dev:run 12-operation demo confirmed all 6 HARD gates and 3 SOFT/always-escalate gates fire as designed. double-close-violation-is-held test specifically audits the dedicated :closed? boolean guard."
  :adr/registry-commit-sha "619b02e7e00f159f1a10f0ccbc00c56ef4903fc1"
  :adr/repos-published ["https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6202"]
  :adr/scope-note "This is a NEW ADR, not an addendum, because ISIC 6202 is outside the scope of every prior cloud-itonami-isic ADR in this superproject, even though it shares the identical governed-actor pattern and reuses ADR-2607071351's double-guard lesson and cloud-itonami-isic-5820's kotoba.crm.pipeline technical commons."}]
